h you for a bit and the response of  Franklin is I guess not and that's one  of the things to know right for those of  you guys who have never dealt with  somebody who's dealing with grief and  grief comes in a lot of different forms  right grief comes in from a variety of  different sources if you've never been  around or dealt with anybody who is  going through grief it's not a matter of  demanding things it's not a matter of  saying this is what you need sometimes  it's just learning how to shut the hell  up and sometimes it's just learning how  to say I'm here if you need me because  sometimes all they want is to just be  there but they also want you want to  know that you're there and that's enough  that that's that's really all it is it's  not problem solving it's not getting  everything sorted out sometimes they  just want to sit there and be quiet and  then they just burst into tears or they  just start screaming and shouting or  something like that because that's what  they need in the moment what Franklin  needs is a friend and the reality here  is everybody is struggling with grief in  their own way that Franklin doesn't  really have anybody to turn to and so  turning to Peter he simply says like my  uncle Johnny died and the response of  Peter is yeah I know I'm very sorry  about that uh how are you doing with all  that stuff and Franklin again is kind of  having a conversation with a kid you  know I'm I'm not doing so well you know  I'm not really sleeping all that well  and I have I'm having bad thoughts I  want to hurt people I want to do bad  things right I want to destroy things  that kind of stuff right and again it's  a pause for concern it's like this is  not like a little kid who's just like  I'm really really angry you know and  it's like well how does that make you  feel you know you know draw on a piece  of paper with a crayon you know it's  like okay Franklin well please don't  destroy all of creation you know it's  that kind of a thing right it's that  kind of concern and so Peter Parker  actually ends up grabbing Franklin and  saying okay well let's go get some lunch  you know like like you know you want to  have you had any lunch or anything and  Franklin's like well I'm not really  hungry and Peter's like well I'm  starving right so let's go let's go get  something right let's spend some time  together and it's literally just Peter  Parker and Franklin Richards hanging out  together it's just them spending time  together because that's what Franklin  needs you just need someone to spend  time with him but at that point Peter  kind of opens up to Franco and says look  I don't know if your mom and dad ever  told you about this but when when I was  younger I lost somebody that was close  to me too you know like we were really  really close like you and your uncle  Johnny were close and and when Franklin  was like well what happened you know the  response to Peter is he was killed in a  robbery of course he's talking about  Uncle Ben and that's a really really  cool moment here because Peter's ability  to empathize with Franklin and to say  like I can understand where you're  coming from I don't know exactly how you  feel because I'm not you and in a lot of  ways how you cared about Uncle Johnny  was different than how I cared about  Uncle Ben or how I saw Uncle Ben I do  know what it's like to lose someone  close to me and the response of Peter is  you know me too you know I'm I'm sad  that happened and not a day goes by that  I don't think about him not a single day  goes by where that doesn't happen but it  doesn't make me sad anymore he says I  mean sure I wish he was still here and  God do I miss him but after a while the  dark thoughts the bad ones like you're  having right now they'll fade away and  you'll spend most of your time thinking  about how much fun you had together and  how much you loved him and so Franklin  of course asks the most logical question  there which is how long before that  happens and the response of Peter is it  takes a while and that's true there's  it'd be nice if it's human beings we  could say okay I've lost a loved one uh  in 30 days I'm gonna feel better in 30  days everything's gonna be okay in this  period of time everything will be better  but the reality here is that things  happen to us as human beings things  happen and it's not always fair and  there's no real Rhyme or Reason to it it  is sometimes it's just things that  happen in this world and there is no  deadline for the grieving process right  there is no amount of time that passes  before definitively everything will be  okay there are people out there who have  lost things that were meaningful to them  and they never recovered they never got  better they never bounced back whereas  there are people who had something bad  happen to them and they bounce back  fairly quickly there's no rules here and  that's what Peter's communicating to  Franklin is there's no rules on how long  it takes before these memories or these  thoughts that you have go away and  they're replaced by positive ones just  know that in time that happens in time  things get better and so Franklin says  can I tell you something can I tell you  a secret Spider-Man and Peter's like  yeah and he says I think I could have  stopped Uncle Johnny from dying now this  is an important thing and one of the  single most important things for  Franklin and it's so ridiculously easy  to overlook right it's so ridiculous and  I'm not I'm not even talking about well  you know he's taking the guilt on  himself no this thought right here this  statement I think I could have stopped  Uncle Johnny from dying you need to keep  that in the back of your head because  that single thought right there that  single motivation governs everything  that happens next every single decision  Franklin makes everything he does when  he's learning how to use his powers when  he's being trained by the man that he  doesn't recognize right the person he  doesn't know we'll cover that in future  foundation when all this stuff is  happening right all these things are  happening this is all governed by that  singular thought but the other part of  this is Franklin could have saved Uncle  Johnny from dying right had he possessed  more control over his abilities and I  don't say that because it's like  Franklin you idiot you know it's really  more of yes he's that powerful but it's  one of those things where this guilt  that he feels is going to be channeled  into something more productive and  Franklin is going to become more  powerful than he's ever been in the  history of Marvel Comics and so the  response with Peter is okay well I  promise I'll keep it to myself can I  tell you a secret and Franklin's  response is yeah and he says I know I  could have stopped my Uncle Ben from  dying and while the question of Peter or  a question of Franklin is why didn't you  you Peter gives this amazing statement  to Franklin which again this is why I  say this conversation is the most  important conversation Franklin's ever  going to have that Peter says because I  was young because I didn't understand  how important every single decision we  make is because I had to learn that when  you have gifts like ours you don't think  about yourself first you think about how  lucky you are to have them and how much  other people need help it's what my  uncle would have wanted from me and it's  what your uncle Johnny would have wanted  from you do you understand what I'm  saying and Franklin's response is yes  and so Peter says okay good now I gotta  get you home but this is a hugely  important conversation because Peter  Parker quite literally turned Franklin  Richards from this Anakin Skywalker  approach right just falling to Darkness  and just becoming this despotic  conqueror of the universe to a character  who's actually going to save everything  in existence because he does Franklin  Richards at the end of this story saves  the universe from complete and total  Annihilation and when I say the Universe  I mean he saved the Universe I mean it  quite literally it's one of the greatest  moments ever in the history of Marvel  Comics and I absolutely love it with  that being said guys we're gonna bring  this video to an end next week we will  be back on Thursday to our regular  Fantastic Four schedule except in that  video we're going to be calling it The  Future Foundation because the name  changes but we're going to bring this to  an end thank you guys for watching and I  will catch you all later  peace
 

